<p>Note 1: Due to the seasonal nature of the Company's business, results for the interim period are not necessarily indicative of the results to be expected for the fiscal year. Note 2: This financial information should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto included in the Company s 10-Q for the period ended November 2, 1996 and 10-K for the period ended February 2, 1996 that were filed with the S.E.C.. Note 3: The Company has approximately $15 million in net operating loss carryforwards.  Had the Company operated on a fully taxed basis, net loss would have been $1.5 million, or $0.20 per share for the quarter ended November 2, 1996, as compared to with $1.8 million, or $ 0.33 per share, for the same period last year.  For the nine months ended November 2, 1996, net loss from continuing operations would have been $4.9 million, or $0.66 per share, as compared to net loss of $3.5 million, or $ 0.66 per share, for the same period last year.</p>
